<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Liberty Wave     unloading   corn	     32,450     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   9,072</p>
<p>				     wheat	    19,306</p>
<p>Cemil Taman	arrived     sunflower meal  2,000     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 222     11/11	 barley	    2,709     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	12/11	 soya	     26,414     U.S.</p>
<p>Volgobal 186     16/11	 bran		1,800     Europe</p>
<p>Grigorus	   26/11	 sorghum+soya+  37,500     U.S.</p>
<p>					 corn</p>
<p>Sagbas 3	   10/12	 barley	    4,600     Europe</p>
<p>Johanis	    17/12	 wheat+soya     60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	20/12	 na		 60,000     U.S.</p>
